#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:3
msgid ""
"This method loads XYZ tile maps from a tile server or local file "
"using :func:`pygmt.datasets.load_tile_map` into a georeferenced form, and "
"plots the tiles as a basemap or overlay using :meth:`pygmt.Figure.grdimage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:7
msgid ""
"**Note**: By default, standard web map tiles served in a Spherical Mercator "
"(EPSG:3857) Cartesian format will be reprojected to a geographic coordinate "
"reference system (OGC:CRS84) and plotted with longitude/latitude bounds when "
"``lonlat=True``. If reprojection is not desired, please set ``lonlat=False`` "
"and provide Spherical Mercator (EPSG:3857) coordinates to the ``region`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

