#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:112
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint.  "
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*).  - "
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180,   "
"i.e., looking from south to north]. - *elevation*: Elevation angle of the "
"viewpoint above the horizon [Default   is 90, i.e., looking straight down at "
"nadir]. - *zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are "
"drawn.   Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. "
"[Default is   at the bottom of the z-axis].  Alternatively, set "
"``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting from the previous "
"plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT syntax for finer "
"control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select an axis location "
"other than the plot origin). See :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#perspective-full` for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:112
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:114
msgid ""
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:117
msgid ""
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180, i.e., "
"looking from south to north]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:119
msgid ""
"*elevation*: Elevation angle of the viewpoint above the horizon [Default is "
"90, i.e., looking straight down at nadir]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:121
msgid ""
"*zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are drawn. "
"Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. [Default is at "
"the bottom of the z-axis]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.15/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:125
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set ``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting "
"from the previous plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT "
"syntax for finer control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select "
"an axis location other than the plot origin). See :gmt-"
